# Code Generation

## Tools in this project

| Tool | Purpose | Source | Output |
|------|---------|--------|--------|
| Hive generator | Type adapters (currently none) | `@HiveType` classes | `*.g.dart` |
| easy_localization generate | Locale keys | `assets/translations/` | `lib/generated/locale_keys.g.dart` |
| Mason | Feature scaffold | `bricks/feature` | feature folder under `lib/features/` |

**Not used:** Freezed, json_serializable, injectable, retrofit, auto_route, riverpod_generator.

## Commands

```bash
# Hive (only if @HiveType classes exist)
dart run build_runner build --delete-conflicting-outputs

# Locale keys (after editing JSON translations)
dart run easy_localization:generate --source-dir ./assets/translations -f keys -o locale_keys.g.dart

# New feature scaffold (ask approval first — may overwrite)
mason get
mason make feature --feature_name order --entity_name Order
```

## Agent rules

- **Never hand-edit** `*.g.dart` or `locale_keys.g.dart`.
- After changing annotated classes, regenerate before analyzing.
- `bricks/**` is excluded from the analyzer — edit brick templates carefully; do not treat generated brick output as production until wired (DI, routes, dummy data).
- `flutter_gen` is configured in `pubspec.yaml` but asset codegen is not the primary workflow — prefer existing shared widgets/assets patterns.
